> opinions?

It depends on how strong you are.  I generally try to carry very little
loot with me when I'm doing anything important (like fighting the wiz,
the quest, or the endgame).  When exploring, I try to carry 20 or so
as a rogue or tourist, 15 as a wizard or valk.  When going in for a big
fight, 40-50 as a rogue, 30-40 as a tourist, 25-30 as a wizard or valk.
Note: this is assuming I have a blessed bag of holding, in which
I keep all but about 10 daggers at a time, usually, and 18 or higher 
strength.  And by the endgame, I usually don't bother carrying daggers 
around as a wizard at all.

I find that it's very helpful to become a stashaholic for the purposes
of carrying around useful stuff.  When I go diving, I bring my weapon(s)
and armor, a get-out-of-trouble scroll, 2-3 healing potions, at most 4 wands,
and 2 rations (4 if a vegetarian), plus a key, unihorn, blindfold, and 
perhaps a tinning kit.  No spellbooks!  Carrying spellbooks bad!
Traveling light really helps you cart around daggers, as well as being
able to collect a bit more loot with each dive.

The endgame, of course, is different.  Generally you're not going to
be collecting a lot of loot, so feel free to stock up before you go.
I'm usually one scroll short of burdened when I go on this task.

YMMV, of course.

